  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/2FB9A3">Definition <span data-tag="2FB9A3">1.2.2.1</span>.</a>MapS@$\bHom _{S}(X,Y)$ Let $S$ be a simplicial set containing vertices $x$ and $y$, and let $\calH $ denote the homotopy category of spaces. We define $\bHom _{S}(x,y) = \bHom _{\rm {h} \it {S}}(x,y) \in \calH $ to be the object of $\calH $ representing the space of maps from $x$ to $y$ in $S$. Here $\rm {h} \it {S}$ denotes the homotopy category of $S$, regarded as a $\calH $-enriched category (Definition <a href="/tag/713A3C" data-tag="713A3C">1.1.5.14</a>). </p>
